  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "transferBadPixelsToMap",
    "file": "librawspeed/src/librawspeed/common/RawImage.cpp",
    "description": "The crash is an assertion abort in RawImageData::transferBadPixelsToMap() caused by trusting packed bad-pixel coordinates in mBadPixelPositions. Each entry is unpacked into 16-bit x/y (pos_x = pos & 0xffff, pos_y = pos >> 16) and then asserted to be within uncropped_dim. For this PoV, at least one bad-pixel entry has y that does not fit in 16 bits of uncropped_dim (or otherwise mismatches dimensions), so the debug assert `pos_y < static_cast<ushort16>(uncropped_dim.y)` fails and aborts. Root cause is missing robust bounds validation/rejection of bad-pixel coordinates before asserting/using them.",
    "conditions": "Data flows from the TIFF/DNG fuzzer input into decoder metadata that populates RawImageData::mBadPixelPositions. During RawDecoder::decodeRaw(), interpolateBadPixels is enabled and raw->fixBadPixels() calls transferBadPixelsToMap(). If mBadPixelPositions contains an out-of-range coordinate (especially with image dimensions or coordinates exceeding 16-bit assumptions), the assert in transferBadPixelsToMap triggers ABRT. This PoV provides such malformed bad-pixel data, causing deterministic abort during bad-pixel map transfer."
  },
